// Optional. This file (and WiFi credentials at build time generally) isn't
// required anymore -- on first boot, the device starts an open access
// point ("esp_neos_bridge") and a setup portal at http://192.168.4.1/
// where you pick a network and enter its password from your phone/laptop.
// That's the recommended path; skip this file entirely if you're fine
// using it.
//
// If you'd still rather set WiFi at build time, copy this file to
// secrets.h (which is gitignored -- never committed, see .gitignore) and
// fill in your real credentials. It's used to seed the device's stored
// credentials exactly once, on the very first boot with no WiFi
// configured yet -- after that, it's ignored, and reconfiguring means
// either the setup portal (hold BOOT for 5s during normal operation to
// return to it) or editing this file has no further effect.
//
// Sensor MACs and friendly names are NOT configured here -- they're
// auto-detected at runtime from the bridge's own paired-sensor list and
// stored in the ESP32's flash (NVS).

#pragma once

#define WIFI_SSID "your-wifi-ssid"
#define WIFI_PASSWORD "your-wifi-password"
